## Recommended Batch 13 (Opus-direct, 2 items, ~30-35K combined)

### Item 1: Job Order Phase 3 — status UI + warranty release gating (T2, ~20-25K)
Closes the job order lifecycle by adding the status-transition UI that consumes the
parts/services/signatures from Batch 12 Item 1.

Files to touch (proposed — re-verify at pre-flight):
- apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/service/job-orders/[id]/job-order-status-actions.tsx —
  NEW Client Component, buttons for the documented JobOrder status transitions:
  received→diagnosing, diagnosing→quoted/in_progress, quoted→approved/cancelled, approved→in_progress,
  in_progress→testing, testing→completed (gated on both signatures present), completed→released.
- apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/service/job-orders/[id]/page.tsx — wire the new
  status-actions component into the header.
- apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/job-order.ts — extend `updateStatus` to enforce the
  testing→completed transition only when customerSignatureUrl + technicianSignatureUrl + signedAt
  are all present. Add explicit allowed-transitions table; reject invalid transitions with BAD_REQUEST.
- apps/web/src/__tests__/job-order.test.ts — extend with ~6 tests for the new gates.

### Item 2: ContactLog global list page (T1, ~10-15K)
Carry-forward from Batch 10/11 candidates. Mirror layout of crm/quotations/page.tsx.

Files to touch:
- apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/(app)/crm/contact-logs/page.tsx — NEW Server Component,
  paginated list with customerId + type filter chips via searchParams + Link, table columns
  [date, type, customer, subject, by]. Uses existing trpc contactLog.list procedure.
- apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/crm.ts — verify contactLog.list accepts customerId + type filters;
  no changes expected, but re-verify input shape at pre-flight per Batch 12 lesson.

